  "body": "## What changed\n\n`.claude/skills/camcraft-mcp/SKILL.md`, tool table (section 4, after `set_tool`), two rows added, copied from `crates/app/src/mcp/cutter_tools.rs` on main:\n\n- `get_tool_cutter_profile { \"tool\": string }`: reads the cutter, neck and shank as a spun half-outline (`[z, r, arc]` points from the tip up to the shank top); `drawn` says whether it is a hand-drawn outline or the one the numbers draw; turning tools have none.\n- `set_tool_cutter_profile { \"tool\": string, \"points\": [[z, r] | [z, r, arc], ...] | null }`: sets the drawn outline, or clears it with `null`; must agree with the tool's numbers, else refused by name; display only (toolpaths and checks keep reading the numbers); one undoable step.\n\n`.claude/PROCESS_VERSION` 17 -> 18 (the skill is a process file).\n\n## Not in this PR (owed)\n\n- `set_tool_cutter_params`: waits on #1012 / #957 (unmerged), so the table does not name it yet.\n- The neck-feeds-the-checks note: waits on the same PRs.\n\n## How tested\n\nDocs-only. `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main --dry-run` plans nothing (no `crates/` file changed). Row text checked against the schema and description in `cutter_tools.rs`.\n\n## Process\n\n- PROCESS_VERSION 18 (this PR). PR #991 also bumps to 18; whichever merges second takes the next number when it merges main.\n- Pinned #681 line for merge time: `PROCESS_VERSION <n> · PR #M · camcraft-mcp skill lists the drawn-cutter tools · forks: normal process sync`\n\nFork synced at v0.17.0 (the branch was cut from upstream/main, which has since moved to v0.18.0 - the new rows are in both).\n\nChangelog: none\n\nRefs #1013\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n\n\n",
